{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275243-how-do-you-make-a-robot","id":1275243,"title":"How do you make a robot?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-12-19T00:01:34-08:00","id":1275243,"title":"How do you make a robot?","content":"what are the spheres needed to make a functioning robot or similar animated construct in other paradigms? I Mean Prime 4 is the obvious.. or spirit 4 but is that it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-19T01:14:04-08:00","id":1275251,"title":"","content":"Matter 4, Prime 4, Forces 3, Mind 5 at minimum for a &quot;science fiction&quot; robot. For more mystical constructs it would vary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-19T05:31:21-08:00","id":1275269,"title":"","content":"It depends on what you want the robot to do, how you want it to look like, and the base materials you use.<br /> <br /> Matter it's great to thinker with the materials, to make them better, to make them interact in unnatural ways, and perhaps to allow your robot to break one or two laws of chemistry/physics<br /> <br /> Matter 4 allows to transform matter into complex patterns. If you built a robot through more or less conventional means you don't need Matter 4. Matter 4 isn't necessary to create an old terminator, but it would help to circunvent the problems with working with flexible materials that happen if you want a more futuristic looking robot (or to create trully fantastical beasts like a robot built of nanobots, like a certain newer terminator).<br /> <br /> Forces 3 maybe coupled with Prime 2 it's needed if you don't want to use a conventional power source for the robot to move. Forces it's also very good to improve the robot's weapons<br /> <br /> Mind 5 it's needed to create a &quot;True AI&quot;. I would think that lesser, not trully sentient, AI would be easier to make but the rules are silent. Mind would also provide all the information your machine would use to work <br /> <br /> Alternatively Spirit 2/4 can be used to call a spirit (Spirit 2) into the robot (Spirit 4 it's needed if the spirit can't posses the robot on it's own). But then you have a weird shamanic/necro robot with an agenda of it's own, and I'm not sure that's the idea. An even weirder proposition for the technoshaman would be to &quot;Awaken&quot; the robot with Spirit 3. It would be a robot inhabited by a robot-spirit that's most likely friendly to you until you anger it.<br /> <br /> Prime 3/4 it's needed to infuse an object of any Rote-like supernatural cualities, and thus would be useful to create sci-fy level robots.<br /> <br /> Those are the basics.<br /> <br /> For some robots you may not need to use magick at all, since we already have robots doing the job of humans. Magick can be used to make the process cheaper, faster and better , and/or to create trully powerful robots that can be used to do stuff that our current robots wouldn't be able to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-19-2018, 08:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-19T05:58:05-08:00","id":1275277,"title":"","content":"Let me try this again, what would be required on a pure sphere level to make a machine that is roughly on par with a human? Not counting any mental effects what would be the spheres needed to say give something strength and dexterity of 2ish with no biological basis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-19T06:55:12-08:00","id":1275282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275243-how-do-you-make-a-robot?p=1275277#post1275277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me try this again, what would be required on a pure sphere level to make a machine that is roughly on par with a human? Not counting any mental effects what would be the spheres needed to say give something strength and dexterity of 2ish with no biological basis?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pure Sphere level as in &quot;0 in all relevant Knowledges/Skills needed to make a robot&quot;? Just take <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1410\" data-vbnamecard=\"1410\">Czernobog</a> post and remove Mind 5 since you don't want to count mental effects<br /> <br /> If you had the Knowledges you could be able to do roughly the same with less. Matter 4 would be more than enough since you would be using a regular power source and no actual Rote-like powers are imbued (no need of Forces nor Prime until you start doing more than tampering with the &quot;body&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-19T07:14:07-08:00","id":1275284,"title":"","content":"<br /> The basic &quot;sicence&quot; of <b>animated inorganic constructs</b> it's, as I understand it:<ul><li>Forces 3 + energy source for the actual movement that makes them &quot;animated&quot; <i>(most robots won't need this 'cause science and bateries, but a Golem likely would)</i>,</li> <li>Matter 4 so it's flexible, articulated, and not a flying/rolling lump of matter <i>(again, robots may not need this because they're already articulated. A well crafted Golem made by someone that know how the human body moves may not need this either)</i>,</li> <li>Mind/Spirit so it's autonomous<i> (unnecessary if you're controling it or, in the case of robots, leave the control to regular programming)</i></li> <li>Prime to &quot;join&quot; the patters of Forces with the mind, so the mind can &quot;control&quot; these patterns...essentially Prime would act as the nervous system, allowing the &quot;robot&quot; to control the cinetic energy that animates it <i>(unnecessary if you're directly controling it)</i></li> </ul>It's debatable if Matter 4 it's necessary to make a construct to be as flexible as a human. Probably Matter 3 and a really good design can already provide the materials with the flexibility and presicion needed to emulate a human perfectly. Science doesn't seem to be so far from creating a robot that's roughly on par with a human, and thus I would think that improving the process and the materials with Matter would be all that's necessary to get there (leaving sentience and intelligence aside).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-19-2018, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-19T20:28:08-08:00","id":1275436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275243-how-do-you-make-a-robot?p=1275284#post1275284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[/LIST]It's debatable if Matter 4 it's necessary to make a construct to be as flexible as a human. Probably Matter 3 and a really good design can already provide the materials with the flexibility and presicion needed to emulate a human perfectly. Science doesn't seem to be so far from creating a robot that's roughly on par with a human, and thus I would think that improving the process and the materials with Matter would be all that's necessary to get there (leaving sentience and intelligence aside).</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue as i understand it is power supply(which forces/prime should cover) and the fact that there's alot of different things that come down to what we'd consider &quot;Dex 2&quot; or a human individual robots seem to each get but putting it together has proven problematic.<br /> <br /> what would people say on the successes to physical traits if you are say building for a robot, I mean AI is clearly the mentals/socials Stamina seems a simple matter of structural capability, but strength and dexterity become harder ones for me to grasp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T06:20:25-08:00","id":1275485,"title":"","content":"I think Strength should be Forces manifested trough the matter. I'm no engineer, but I know lots of machines employ hydraulic or magnetic presure to move stuff, which falls under the purview of Forces.<br /> <br /> Dexterity it's more complex to me because there's even a mental component (eye-hand coordination, for instance). Yet if Life it's enough to improve one's dexterity, I would say Forces + a good, articulate, structure should suffice. I would use Forces + Matter to increase the dextrety of an existing robot because it's not just fine-tuned movement, but also the capability to express it trough the structure (flexible and articulate robots at least <i>seem </i>more dextrerous than <a href=\"http://blogficticio2014.blogspot.com/2014/11/tobor-el-grande.html\" target=\"_blank\">Tobor</a>-like robots).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-20-2018, 09:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T07:08:15-08:00","id":1275497,"title":"","content":"Life 5, Matter 3-4, Mind 5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T07:30:53-08:00","id":1275506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275243-how-do-you-make-a-robot?p=1275497#post1275497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Life 5, Matter 3-4, Mind 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where does Life come into it? I guess that would be required if you were creating a <i>cyborg</i>, but a purely robotic or golem-esque entity would require only Matter.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-23T22:06:10-08:00","id":1276377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275243-how-do-you-make-a-robot?p=1275506#post1275506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where does Life come into it? I guess that would be required if you were creating a <i>cyborg</i>, but a purely robotic or golem-esque entity would require only Matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Life has more to do with the type of pattern than it does the material. It's a Living, animate, pattern. Therefore, it's life.<br /> <br /> Life as Flesh, Blood, and Organs is entirely paradigmatic. If your paradigm can conceive of living things that are not composed of flesh then your paradigm can create such things. I would personally err on the side of lower matter sphere requirements solely because you're turning Inanimate Matter Patterns into an Animate Life Pattern.<br /> <br /> It seems rather silly to me to simply arbitrarily decide that 'Life can't do that' because a robot isn't flesh blood and organs despite in all ways resembling a living thing otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11744,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","user":"Enginseer-42","date":". 12-24-2018, 01:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-26T05:31:04-08:00","id":1276774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275243-how-do-you-make-a-robot?p=1276377#post1276377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Life has more to do with the type of pattern than it does the material. It's a Living, animate, pattern. Therefore, it's life.<br /> <br /> It seems rather silly to me to simply arbitrarily decide that 'Life can't do that' because a robot isn't flesh blood and organs despite in all ways resembling a living thing otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more silly to think that 'stuff moving on it's own' it's what defines Life. Sorry, but I can't accept that it's a &quot;Living pattern&quot; just because it's animated<br /> <br /> All sorts of matter move on it's own. Magnets move on their own when you place certan substances near them. In fact ALL matter in the universe it's animated trough gravity among other forces - Forces controls movement. Life it's most often defined as following the 'cycle of life' of birth , growth, reproduction and death.<br /> <br /> Robots don't eat, crap, fuck and die. All sophistry saying that robot's &quot;eat energy&quot;, reproduce trough human enginery and die when their parts decay can't truly distinguish robots from falling rocks (who also start moving at a point, may be reproduced by humans throwing more rocks, and die when their movement it's over). Most sci-fy Robots are little more than puppets. They aren't alive to any sensible definition of life until you add a Mind that can think about stuff like being alive and reproduce - and that's already done trough Mind 5, no need to add Life to the equation. <hr /><br /> Besides, Life sphere it's very, VERY, clear about it affecting &quot;living organic stuff&quot;. All Life levels describe effects affecting organic living beings. And while Life becomes Matter at the moment of death, no place in the book says that the cycle also goes the other way with inorganic stuff becoming Life (The methaphysics of magick define the interaction of patterns, and the arrows point the way. It's a one way street).<br /> <br /> Think about the implications. If you don't accept that robots aren't alive then you will be forced to allow players to mutate or repair an Uber self-driving car with Life Sphere.<br /> <br /> You can't let Paradigm define the OOC System you're using to play the game. Think about the implications: soon you will have players doing everything trough Forces because everything in the universe it's just energy moving arround.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-26-2018, 08:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-26T10:11:14-08:00","id":1276819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275243-how-do-you-make-a-robot?p=1276774#post1276774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...)<br /> You can't let Paradigm define the OOC System you're using to play the game. Think about the implications: soon you will have players doing everything trough Forces because everything in the universe it's just energy moving arround.</div> </div> </div> </div>A whole book could be written about such errors. About how Mages make mistakes, cause mishaps, stumble in all sorts of ways, and misunderstand what they have discovered or been told about ; and the consequences ( the bad, and the possible good ones ) that this leads to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-26T10:49:17-08:00","id":1276824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275243-how-do-you-make-a-robot?p=1276819#post1276819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A whole book could be written about such errors. About how Mages make mistakes, cause mishaps, stumble in all sorts of ways, and misunderstand what they have discovered or been told about ; and the consequences ( the bad, and the possible good ones ) that this leads to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, Mages can't mistake what &quot;Sphere&quot; to use because their belief shapes reality, and more than reality it shapes the way they do their own magick. If they believe their magick works X way then it works X way. If a Mage believes &quot;Quintessence&quot; it's a &quot;Force&quot; then he can totally erase patterns and create Talismans with &quot;Forces&quot;. If a Mage believes &quot;Spheres&quot; are a nonsense invented by the Hermetics and don't exist, then they don't exist and he can do whatever he wants without having to learn any &quot;Spheres&quot; whatsoever. That is, IOC, <b>Inside of Character</b>...<br /> <br /> <i>...Meanwhile, OOC, <b>Outside of Character,</b> The Player, not the Mage, knows that he is using the Sphere of Prime as the Book and STs demand.</i><br /> <br /> So, as you see, no books should be written about these mistakes because that's what the Corebook of Mage it's all about. It's not a mistake of mages but of players/ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-26-2018, 01:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-26T11:11:44-08:00","id":1276830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275243-how-do-you-make-a-robot?p=1276824#post1276824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really, Mages can't mistake what &quot;Sphere&quot; to use because their belief shapes reality, and more than reality it shapes the way they do their own magick. If they believe their magick works X way then it works X way.<br /> (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Mages can make mistakes within this. Their beliefs can be uncertain, incomplete, not strong enough, or contradictory. Also, there is a baseline reality, and trends within it, that the a Mage should adhere to within her ( or his ) beliefs and approach to Magick ; with negative consequences following if she does not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-27T05:56:49-08:00","id":1276982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275243-how-do-you-make-a-robot?p=1276830#post1276830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Mages can make mistakes within this. Their beliefs can be uncertain, incomplete, not strong enough, or contradictory. Also, there is a baseline reality, and trends within it, that the a Mage should adhere to within her ( or his ) beliefs and approach to Magick ; with negative consequences following if she does not.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're missing my point here. I think you're right <i>in general</i>, but not about the relationship between the Spheres and Paradigm.<br /> <br /> Let me give the example I always give when this comes up: The Sisters of Hippolyta.<br /> <br /> It's clearly stated in the book of crafts and the ST guide that they refused to join the Traditions because they refuse to believe that magick it's sepparated in Spheres.<br /> <br /> They are adamant about magick being indivisible , and thus they don't have alternate names for the Spheres because they don't believe in the Spheres. It's clearly stated that they use only ONE &quot;source&quot; of magick, which won't even fit in the Pillars system of DA (which would demand them to divide their magick in four parts rather than nine - which they wouldn't accept either).<br /> <br /> So the Sisters use ONE Sphere/Pillar/Whatever for everything. And it works like a charm - they never had a single problem casting a spell or attaining all the varied powers of magick users.<br /> <br /> And this is because regardless of what IOC cardboard fictional characters are supposed to believe, OOC their player will use the game system as everyone else, and not because &quot;a baseline reality&quot; or any other methaphisical nonsense.<br /> <br /> <u>Mage it's NOT Reality It's an RPG:</u> it's &quot;baseline reality&quot; doesn't define the Systems you use, the Sistems you use define Mage's &quot;baseline reality&quot; which doesn't exist outside these systems and the fluff that acompanies them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-27-2018, 09:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-27T16:53:10-08:00","id":1277117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275243-how-do-you-make-a-robot?p=1276774#post1276774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's more silly to think that 'stuff moving on it's own' it's what defines Life. Sorry, but I can't accept that it's a &quot;Living pattern&quot; just because it's animated<br /> <br /> All sorts of matter move on it's own. Magnets move on their own when you place certan substances near them. In fact ALL matter in the universe it's animated trough gravity among other forces - Forces controls movement. Life it's most often defined as following the 'cycle of life' of birth , growth, reproduction and death.<br /> <br /> Robots don't eat, crap, fuck and die. All sophistry saying that robot's &quot;eat energy&quot;, reproduce trough human enginery and die when their parts decay can't truly distinguish robots from falling rocks (who also start moving at a point, may be reproduced by humans throwing more rocks, and die when their movement it's over). Most sci-fy Robots are little more than puppets. They aren't alive to any sensible definition of life until you add a Mind that can think about stuff like being alive and reproduce - and that's already done trough Mind 5, no need to add Life to the equation. <hr /><br /> Besides, Life sphere it's very, VERY, clear about it affecting &quot;living organic stuff&quot;. All Life levels describe effects affecting organic living beings. And while Life becomes Matter at the moment of death, no place in the book says that the cycle also goes the other way with inorganic stuff becoming Life (The methaphysics of magick define the interaction of patterns, and the arrows point the way. It's a one way street).<br /> <br /> Think about the implications. If you don't accept that robots aren't alive then you will be forced to allow players to mutate or repair an Uber self-driving car with Life Sphere.<br /> <br /> You can't let Paradigm define the OOC System you're using to play the game. Think about the implications: soon you will have players doing everything trough Forces because everything in the universe it's just energy moving arround.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not really. Magnets don't move under direction. They move as FORCES dictate they move. That's a force combined with matter. Not a living pattern. A robot meanwhile will move with direction. It won't simply fall, or be pulled by magnetism in a single direction or at the whims of its environment it will move with it's own internal purpose and logic.<br /> <br /> Eating, crapping, fucking, and dying are all irrelevant to being alive.<br /> <br /> And? Mage has canonically accepted spontanious generation of old as an explanation paradigmatically and had magical effects key off it. Where flies just appear because you left something out and aren't living creatures that breed on their own. The idea that our modern ideas of biology are baked into the reality of magic is nonsensical to the nth degree.<br /> <br /> And quite frankly, most definitions of LIFE are sophistry, we don't have an adequate explanation of what alive is because we've never really had much to defy the basics. Robots are one of those things that defy the basics.<br /> <br /> 90% of ants don't personally reproduce, they have an organic factory in the form of the queen that does that for them. Does that make ants less alive? Most living bodies are little more than puppets without a mind to guide them.<br /> <br /> Your entire argument can be thrown back at you as equally applying to every living thing on the planet. The only difference is the material they are constructed of, and the means by which they fuel and self repair.<br /> <br /> Nonsensical. You eat dead things, dead things become part of you, at which point a matter pattern becomes part of a living pattern. OR you attach a part to a robot.<br /> <br /> Also yes. If they believed that to be possible and the self driving car was made with the life sphere. If their paradigm doesn't accept non-organic life (Verbena) then obviously it wouldn't work. And if their paradigm did accept such, it still wouldn't be 'mutation' it would be reconstruction. Modification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-28T13:39:25-08:00","id":1277248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not really. Magnets don't move under direction. They move as FORCES dictate they move. That's a force combined with matter. Not a living pattern. A robot meanwhile will move with direction. It won't simply fall, or be pulled by magnetism in a single direction or at the whims of its environment it will move with it's own internal purpose and logic. </div> </div> </div>Electro-magnets can be activated and deactivated on comand, and can produce complex movement on such comands - they effectively move upon my directions transmited by a button or other devise, which can be as simple as a lever or as complex as a cortical implant on my brain.<br /> <br /> In a robot all the logic it's in the program, which it's just a set of instructions that are to be followed that aren't different from pulling a series of levers. Programs were originally analogic (cards or valves), so, as you see, this isn't an exageration: A sufficently complex system of YES/NOP levers could achieve most of the same function of an actual IA inside a gigantic robot. Self learning would be a problem because you would need a way to crate more levers or change them somehow, but an AI it's not beyond &quot;Turing compatible&quot; as far as I know, and thus it's not really beyond levers or other types of logic doors.<br /> <br /> So, according to your &quot;method&quot;, flying swords that you control with your mind it's Forces + Matter, but flying swords that have a fixed set of instructions are Life + Matter?. I would think not. Normal robots aren't that much different from these. And with magickal robots the difference it's Mind 5 allowing to go a little beyond logic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And? Mage has canonically accepted spontanious generation of old as an explanation paradigmatically and had magical effects key off it. Where flies just appear because you left something out and aren't living creatures that breed on their own. The idea that our modern ideas of biology are baked into the reality of magic is nonsensical to the nth degree.<br /> <br /> And quite frankly, most definitions of LIFE are sophistry, we don't have an adequate explanation of what alive is because we've never really had much to defy the basics. Robots are one of those things that defy the basics.<br /> <br /> 90% of ants don't personally reproduce, they have an organic factory in the form of the queen that does that for them. Does that make ants less alive? Most living bodies are little more than puppets without a mind to guide them.<br /> <br /> Your entire argument can be thrown back at you as equally applying to every living thing on the planet. The only difference is the material they are constructed of, and the means by which they fuel and self repair.<br /> <br /> Nonsensical. You eat dead things, dead things become part of you, at which point a matter pattern becomes part of a living pattern. OR you attach a part to a robot. </div> </div> </div>You're totally right that science doesn't define what magick does. However, Mage has systems to define what magick does and there are clear and defined parameters that won't depend on what your Paradigm says. You need Matter to conjute Life out of garbage, you need Prime to conjure it from Quintessence, you need Spirit/DimSci to affect an &quot;alien&quot; from the Umbra, even if you believe the E.T it's a living being like any other.<br /> <br /> I want to higlight a part of your argument:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your entire argument can be thrown back at you as equally applying to every living thing on the planet.<b> The only difference is the material they are constructed of, and the means by which they fuel and self repair.</b> </div> </div> </div>See, here you've demolished your own argument in a much trough way than I could have imagined. Thanks for throwing my weak argument back at me with so much more destructive power<br /> <br /> So, the only difference between Humans and Robots it's their fuel and self repair... YES ...<br /> <br /> ...y<i>et to affect the limbs of cyborg with Magick <u><b>RAW</b></u> you need Matter + Life while to affect a normal human Life alone it's more than enough</i> (and this for Technocrats and Technomances, not Verbena, as per the Book): Doesn't a cyborg arm move trough the internal logic of the cyborg?, then why it's in any way different from a normal arm?, why Life alone isn't enough?.<br /> <br /> You HAVE to admit that the system recognizes a difference between Life and Matter that goes beyond &quot;moving trough it's own internal purpose and logic&quot; because this difference doesn't exist between cyborgs and humans in your so called counterargument, and yet the system, RAW, makes a difference.<br /> <br /> The only explanation, under this Paradigm, it's its composition, or maybe the fuel/regeneration.<br /> <br /> And cyborgs are more akin to an organic beings than robots are, hence, following your so called anty-paradigm...<i>perhaps robots won't need Life at all?</i> =). <hr /><br /> My point being, leaving all sophistry aside: The System defines what Life does, and the System clearly talks about biological stuff in every level: Every level of Life it's defined and exemplified affecting organic, biological, beings, up to the point that &quot;undead&quot; aren't living enough to be affected by Life alone even when they're both organic AND moving. <br /> <br /> Do you see a level or an example in ANY book whatsoever of Life being used to mutate or create a Robot?. I doubt so, and until you prove me wrong anyone will notice that <u>you can't do this</u>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also yes. If they believed that to be possible<b><u> and </u>the self driving car was made with the life sphere.</b> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>And how it's that only the self-driving cars made with the Life Sphere are alive?</i>. </span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Or suddenly only robots made by Mages count as alive?</span></b><br /> <br /> If you can affect robots with Life then you can affect ALL self-driving cars AND ALL computers that harbor even the simplests of IA, even cellphones, with Life.<u> If you can create an intelligent phone without Life then I can effectively, <i>and with absolute certainty</i>, create Robots without Life.</u> Even those with an advanced IA, since that's just Mind 5.<br /> <br /> I just need to create the sentient phone and connect it to an inanimated Robot made with Matter trough the regular firmware that most machine use. Even funnier: Now that I've created the robot w/o a single dot of Life, because you define Life as willful movement, my robot &quot;transforms&quot; into a Life pattern the moment I put the sentient phone and back to Matter when I remove the sentient phone. Fun, isn't it?. Ideal for repairs, since I don't have a single dot of Life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 12-28-2018, 05:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-28T14:47:29-08:00","id":1277264,"title":"","content":"I mean, if you want to make a robot out of nanomachines that can mimic a living being T-1000 style, I can definitely seeing Life being necessary. Just not in most cases of making a robot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-29T06:56:33-08:00","id":1277349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275243-how-do-you-make-a-robot?p=1276774#post1276774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Besides, Life sphere it's very, VERY, clear about it affecting &quot;living organic stuff&quot;. All Life levels describe effects affecting organic living beings. And while Life becomes Matter at the moment of death, no place in the book says that the cycle also goes the other way with inorganic stuff becoming Life (The methaphysics of magick define the interaction of patterns, and the arrows point the way. It's a one way street).</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a certain logic to it, which I would be willing to listen to as an ST. A mage still needs Life (in addition to Matter) to do anything with necromancy, at least in the sense of fucking around with the undead as opposed to ghosts or other entropic spirits. It wouldn't be the first case of Sphere overlap -- case in point, Entropy, spirits of entropy and death, and the &quot;underworld&quot;. Or, for that matter, Mind, the astral plane, and the spirits which inhabit it.<br /> <br /> What a more orthodox interpretation of Life yields, is the sphere grants mastery over animate, self-sustaining and -replicating, Patterns compromised of organic compounds that are organized by cells. So we've established what is a &quot;Life Pattern&quot;; that's all well and good for <i>most</i> circumstances, but that still gets a little murky on the fringes. The books are pretty clear Life covers prokaryotes and viruses, but what about prions and ribozymes, or even enzymes in a vacuum? We can infer &quot;yes&quot;, but the logic behind it gets a little iffy when you stop and <i>really</i> think about it.<br /> <br /> So, what if we have a Progenitor stationed aboard a Voidship, who decides a Really Neat Experiment would be to design a lifeform that could survive on Titan? Methanogenic life that synthesizes acetylene instead of glucose, etc. We're still dealing with organic compounds, so no brainer, right?<br /> <br /> Well, what if instead of Titan, that Progenitor starts their little experiment for Venus, or more appropriately as Venus is too cold, what astronomers currently believe Kepler-96c to be? Well, we're talking about silicon-based life that metabolizes silicates and sulfurates about which we can hypothesize the chemistry, however unlikely it is to be in the universe. They'd definitely need Matter and Prime to get the ball rolling (and DimSci for obvious reasons), but once our hypothetical Progenitor gets the compounds to a point of self-replication, at what point (if any) would Life then apply?<br /> <br /> So, that's within the realm of &quot;chemistry we've been able to figure out, or at least hypothesize about&quot;. Let's start talking about the <b><i>REALLY </i></b>weird shit. Ten or fifteen years ago there was an experiment with argon plasma to replicate early-Earth atmospheric conditions. What happened, was the plasma formed cell-like structures that were actually capable of growing, self-replicating, and exchanging information with other structures. So now we have the (remote) possibility of some kind of weird-ass prokaryotic-ish(?) <i>plasma</i>-based life that could proliferate in gas giants and brown dwarves perhaps, go figure. What the fuck kind of spheres you'd use for that, I could only speculate, but we're at the point of <i>Forces</i> taking primacy over Spirit, Mind, or even Matter, as a conjunctional Sphere to Life.<br /> <br /> Really, &quot;Life&quot; in these terms has basically the same definition as &quot;porn&quot;: you know it when you see it. Well, in this case in my opinion, the <i>Consensus</i> knows it when it sees it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-30T10:28:15-08:00","id":1277519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1275243-how-do-you-make-a-robot?p=1277248#post1277248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Electro-magnets can be activated and deactivated on comand, and can produce complex movement on such comands - they effectively move upon my directions transmited by a button or other devise, which can be as simple as a lever or as complex as a cortical implant on my brain.<br /> <br /> In a robot all the logic it's in the program, which it's just a set of instructions that are to be followed that aren't different from pulling a series of levers. Programs were originally analogic (cards or valves), so, as you see, this isn't an exageration: A sufficently complex system of YES/NOP levers could achieve most of the same function of an actual IA inside a gigantic robot. Self learning would be a problem because you would need a way to crate more levers or change them somehow, but an AI it's not beyond &quot;Turing compatible&quot; as far as I know, and thus it's not really beyond levers or other types of logic doors.<br /> <br /> So, according to your &quot;method&quot;, flying swords that you control with your mind it's Forces + Matter, but flying swords that have a fixed set of instructions are Life + Matter?. I would think not. Normal robots aren't that much different from these. And with magickal robots the difference it's Mind 5 allowing to go a little beyond logic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You're totally right that science doesn't define what magick does. However, Mage has systems to define what magick does and there are clear and defined parameters that won't depend on what your Paradigm says. You need Matter to conjute Life out of garbage, you need Prime to conjure it from Quintessence, you need Spirit/DimSci to affect an &quot;alien&quot; from the Umbra, even if you believe the E.T it's a living being like any other.<br /> <br /> I want to higlight a part of your argument:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> See, here you've demolished your own argument in a much trough way than I could have imagined. Thanks for throwing my weak argument back at me with so much more destructive power<br /> <br /> So, the only difference between Humans and Robots it's their fuel and self repair... YES ...<br /> <br /> ...y<i>et to affect the limbs of cyborg with Magick <u><b>RAW</b></u> you need Matter + Life while to affect a normal human Life alone it's more than enough</i> (and this for Technocrats and Technomances, not Verbena, as per the Book): Doesn't a cyborg arm move trough the internal logic of the cyborg?, then why it's in any way different from a normal arm?, why Life alone isn't enough?.<br /> <br /> You HAVE to admit that the system recognizes a difference between Life and Matter that goes beyond &quot;moving trough it's own internal purpose and logic&quot; because this difference doesn't exist between cyborgs and humans in your so called counterargument, and yet the system, RAW, makes a difference.<br /> <br /> The only explanation, under this Paradigm, it's its composition, or maybe the fuel/regeneration.<br /> <br /> And cyborgs are more akin to an organic beings than robots are, hence, following your so called anty-paradigm...<i>perhaps robots won't need Life at all?</i> =). <hr /><br /> My point being, leaving all sophistry aside: The System defines what Life does, and the System clearly talks about biological stuff in every level: Every level of Life it's defined and exemplified affecting organic, biological, beings, up to the point that &quot;undead&quot; aren't living enough to be affected by Life alone even when they're both organic AND moving.<br /> <br /> Do you see a level or an example in ANY book whatsoever of Life being used to mutate or create a Robot?. I doubt so, and until you prove me wrong anyone will notice that <u>you can't do this</u>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><i>And how it's that only the self-driving cars made with the Life Sphere are alive?</i>. </span><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Or suddenly only robots made by Mages count as alive?</span></b><br /> <br /> If you can affect robots with Life then you can affect ALL self-driving cars AND ALL computers that harbor even the simplests of IA, even cellphones, with Life.<u> If you can create an intelligent phone without Life then I can effectively, <i>and with absolute certainty</i>, create Robots without Life.</u> Even those with an advanced IA, since that's just Mind 5.<br /> <br /> I just need to create the sentient phone and connect it to an inanimated Robot made with Matter trough the regular firmware that most machine use. Even funnier: Now that I've created the robot w/o a single dot of Life, because you define Life as willful movement, my robot &quot;transforms&quot; into a Life pattern the moment I put the sentient phone and back to Matter when I remove the sentient phone. Fun, isn't it?. Ideal for repairs, since I don't have a single dot of Life.</div> </div> </div> </div>And your nervous system moves your limbs by a sequence of electrical impulses to muscle materials that then either relax or contract. All under the guiding logic of it's own blueprint contained within DNA.<br /> <br /> Organic Bodies are no less mechanical. A human body is a carefully organized bundle of Oxygen, Carbon, Hydrogen, Nitrogen, Calcium, Phosphorus, Potassium, Sulfur, Sodium, Chlorine, and Magnesium<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">. Give or take some Trace elements.<br /> <br /> Do any of those seem particularly alive? Would you govern any of those with Life? Or Would you govern them with Matter? <br /> <br /> Life as a sphere has to do with constructions. A BODY with self contained systems. Like for example, a robot, or a human, or a dog.<br /> <br /> Also, you need no such thing. The Verbena's standard trick is to fuck over cyborgs with life alone. You need LIFE to make cybernetics. Not matter. Because Cybernetics are just a variation of the Better Body rote. The Biomechanics chosen sphere is LIFE. Not matter.<br /> <br /> Also YES. As mentioned the Biomechanics, the 'Cyborgs and Robots' guys of the Union build all these things with life.<br /> <br /> And no, no you can't because there is a difference between a robot and a self driving car. One is a Mind within an Object. the other is a body with it's own internal construction that allows it all to move together with purpose (Potentially with or without a mind)<br /> <br /> So you're again, attaching a mind to an inanimate object. Not building a robotic body with life. Certainly, you could get something out of that approach, but it wouldn't be the same nor would it be as effective. You would not be creating a creature with stats and potentially skills talents/abilities of it's own. You'd be giving an inanimate object a mind.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-02T05:38:03-08:00","id":1278048,"title":"","content":"I'm with Aleph on this one. It doesn't matter which in universe sphere, pillar, principle or whatever a Mage thinks they are using it doesn't change what sphere we use OOC because the OOC spheres are just gaming systems. When approaches are so different they demand a drastically different rule set the books sometimes use a variant Sphere like Data or Primal utility, but that is a kludge. I wouldn't use those as a blueprint for how Paradigm affects Spheres because that leads to the mess that was HDYDT. <br /> <br /> Likewise there's nothing informative about Cybernetics using the Better Body rote, it's just a convenient and simple way of handling things at the table. A cybernetic arm requires Life because it is made to work and interact with living systems. That's the impossible thing about it that requires technocratic &quot;science&quot;. If it doesn't do that it isn't cybernetic* just a robot arm on a table somewhere. <br /> <br /> *by the popular usage of the term.<br /> <br /> I'm certainly open to the idea of technological or non-organic things falling under the Life purview but there has to be a reason. They have to fit the definitions of life in a meaningful way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-03T12:37:55-08:00","id":1278379,"title":"","content":"The issue with that is that, as mentioned variant spheres exist. <br /> Implying that paradigm does have an effect. Where HDYDT went wrong isn't in allowing paradigm influence magic, but in taking the M20 Standard of including every possible sphere needed at the highest potential level needed. Not mention definitions of life tend to be more or less nonsensical. Under many common definitions fire counts as a living thing. Usually to avoid things like that people try to redefine it as being made of cells or flesh or whatever but that is frankly a cop out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-04T08:09:41-08:00","id":1278587,"title":"","content":"Fire does not maintain homeostasis nor is it organized, two of the most important elements of life. Also for the purposes of Mage it mystically, scientifically, and colloquially belongs to the Forces sphere.<br /> <br /> It seems to me you are falling into the continuum fallacy here. Just because the definition of Life is more vague than we would like doesn't mean it is nonsensical. Life is an organized system that metabolizes, grows, and maintains homeostasis, or to put that in non scientific terms it is grows, adapts, perpetuates, and maintains itself. Yes, despite your earlier statement eating (and to a lesser extent crapping) are very relevant to life.<br /> <br /> You can get to machines that do approach Life as we understand it, but they start to look like the Replicators from Stargate or the more advanced Transformers. The self driving cars from earlier don't qualify because self driving cars don't heal, or consume and synthesize materials to maintain their integrity, or any of a number of complicated things that even the most basic of single celled organisms constantly do.<br /> <br /> If you had a self driving car that did, though, I'd say it would be reasonable to heal it with Life.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The issue with HDYDT is that it included Spheres that did nothing for the spell just because it sounded good. So Pyrokinesis required Mind despite the fact that it is functionally indistinguishable from a basic Forces 3/Prime 2 spell. The point of the Spheres system is that you can use it for almost any kind of magic without changing the rules. Paradigm does not affect the spheres you use because paradigm is an in universe belief system and spheres are a gaming abstraction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 01-04-2019, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}